cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this driver, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "instamatic-dcx-driver: a Rust driver for DECTRIS SINGLA detectors in Instamatic"
authors:
  - family-names: Tsai
    given-names: Chung-Han
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3581-7654"
version: 1.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23993707
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/qitsweauca-dcx/instamatic-dcx-driver"
abstract: >-
  A camera interface for Instamatic, and for programs built on it, that drives a DECTRIS SINGLA
  through its detector control unit: the SIMPLON 1.8 REST API for control, Stream V2 over ZeroMQ
  for the frames, and the Monitor for the live view. It is written in Rust and loaded by Python as
  one extension module; frames are decoded and decompressed (bslz4, lz4) without holding Python's
  GIL. It supports single images, movies and continuous series in the trigger modes ints, inte,
  exts and exte. DECTRIS, SINGLA and SIMPLON are names of DECTRIS Ltd; this project is not made,
  endorsed or supported by DECTRIS.
keywords:
  - electron diffraction
  - 3D ED
  - Instamatic
  - DECTRIS SINGLA
  - SIMPLON
  - Stream V2
  - ZeroMQ
  - camera driver
  - Rust
